@theseOnAuthServer_HostAddress = https://localhost:7146

### Register with username, email, and password
POST {{theseOnAuthServer_HostAddress}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "a-long-example-password"
}

### Log in with username or email and issue OpenIddict tokens
POST {{theseOnAuthServer_HostAddress}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=theseOnAuthServer&username=alice&password=a-long-example-password&scope=openid%20profile%20email

### Start SPA login in a browser (generate PKCE S256 challenge, state, and nonce in the SPA)
GET {{theseOnAuthServer_HostAddress}}/connect/authorize?client_id=theseOnOAuth&response_type=code&redirect_uri=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5174%2Fauth%2Fcallback&scope=openid%20profile%20email&code_challenge={{code_challenge}}&code_challenge_method=S256&state={{state}}&nonce={{nonce}}

### Exchange the authorization code in the SPA using its original code_verifier
POST {{theseOnAuthServer_HostAddress}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&client_id=theseOnOAuth&redirect_uri=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5174%2Fauth%2Fcallback&code={{authorization_code}}&code_verifier={{code_verifier}}

### Request a magic link (SMTP and MagicLinks:CallbackUrl must be configured)
POST {{theseOnAuthServer_HostAddress}}/auth/magic-link
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com"
}

### Exchange the token from the email callback URL (single-use)
POST {{theseOnAuthServer_HostAddress}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=magic_link&client_id=theseOnAuthServer&magic_token={{magic_link_token}}&scope=openid%20profile%20email
